Today the stack is approximately

\text{skfolio}
\rightarrow
\text{CVXPY}
\rightarrow
\text{OSQP/Clarabel}
\rightarrow
\text{linear algebra}.

Your accelerated WalkForward work is exploiting an important property:

P_{t+1}\approx P_t.

The solver should therefore not see

P_1,P_2,\ldots,P_T

as independent programs.

It should see

P(\theta_1)
\rightarrow
P(\theta_2)
\rightarrow
\cdots
\rightarrow
