5. ADMM becomes particularly natural

Suppose MeanRisk canonicalizes into

\min_{x,z}
f_t(x)+g(z)

with

Ax+Bz=c.

Then retain

(x_t,z_t,u_t)

between consecutive problems.

For the next problem:

(x_t,z_t,u_t)
\rightarrow
(x_{t+1},z_{t+1},u_{t+1}).

You don’t start ADMM again.

You are tracking the solution manifold.

For a slowly changing covariance matrix, you can potentially retain much more:

K_t=A^\top A+\rho I,

and if only numerical coefficients change, update or reuse the relevant factorization rather than reconstructing everything.

That is a much stronger optimization than simply saying warm_start=True.

